<http://example.org/process/support-to-the-digital-transition> skos:prefLabel "Support to the digital transition"@en .

<http://example.org/standard/member-states-shall-have-systems-and-procedures-in-place-to-ensure-that-all-supporting-documents-necessary-for-the-audit-trail-related-to-a-measure-supported-by-the-fund-are-kept-at-the-appropriate-level-for-a-10-year-period-from-31-december-of-the-year-in-which-the-last-payment-by-the-commission-to-the-member-state-is-made-where-a-redress-procedure-has-been-initiated-an-appeal-has-been-lodged-or-where-court-proceedings-have-begun-the-supporting-documents-shall-be-kept-until-those-procedures-or-any-subsequent-recovery-procedures-are-terminated> a dcterms:Standard ;
    dcterms:title "Member States shall have systems and procedures in place to ensure that all supporting documents necessary for the audit trail related to a measure supported by the Fund are kept at the appropriate level for a 10-year period from 31 December of the year in which the last payment by the Commission to the Member State is made; where a redress procedure has been initiated, an appeal has been lodged or where court proceedings have begun, the supporting documents shall be kept until those procedures or any subsequent recovery procedures are terminated;"@en .

<http://example.org/standard/the-commission-shall-publish-this-data-subject-to-exceptions-provided-for-by-the-regulation-on-a-centralised-website-with-the-share-of-union-contribution-referred-to-in-the-performance-regulation-information-on-name-and-surname-in-case-of-a-natural-person-or-name-in-case-of-a-legal-entity-shall-not-be-published-if-the-amount-received-by-them-in-one-year-is-equal-to-or-less-than-eur-2500> a dcterms:Standard ;
    dcterms:title "The Commission shall publish this data, subject to exceptions provided for by the regulation, on a centralised website with the share of Union contribution referred to in the [Performance regulation]. Information on name and surname, in case of a natural person, or name, in case of a legal entity, shall not be published, if the amount received by them in one year is equal to or less than EUR 2500."@en .

<http://example.org/standard/the-information-shall-be-updated-at-least-every-six-months-the-information-on-the-calls-for-proposals-shall-be-updated-at-least-two-times-a-year> a dcterms:Standard ;
    dcterms:title "The information shall be updated at least every six months. The information on the calls for proposals shall be updated at least two times a year."@en .

<http://example.org/standard/these-systems-shall-include-among-others-use-of-automatic-and-interactive-forms-and-calculations-ensure-record-keeping-and-data-storage-in-the-system-enabling-both-administrative-verifications-of-payment-claims-submitted-by-beneficiaries-and-audits-as-well-as-allow-for-automatic-synchronisation-and-transmission-of-data-between-beneficiaries-and-member-states-systems> a dcterms:Standard ;
    dcterms:title "These systems shall include, among others, use of automatic and interactive forms and calculations, ensure record-keeping and data storage in the system enabling both administrative verifications of payment claims submitted by beneficiaries and audits as well as allow for automatic synchronisation and transmission of data between beneficiaries' and Member States' systems."@en .

<http://example.org/standard/this-data-should-be-in-at-least-one-of-the-official-language-or-languages-of-the-member-state-andor-in-either-english-french-or-german-and-shall-remain-available-on-the-website-for-two-years-from-the-date-of-its-initial-publication-the-data-published-on-the-website-shall-be-a-digital-ready-open-interoperable-and-machine-readable-format-which-allows-data-to-be-sorted-searched-extracted-compared-and-reused> a dcterms:Standard ;
    dcterms:title "This data should be in at least one of the official language or languages of the Member State and/or in either English, French or German and shall remain available on the website for two years from the date of its initial publication. The data published on the website shall be a digital-ready, open, interoperable and machine-readable format, which allows data to be sorted, searched, extracted, compared and reused."@en .

